# Backend Rules

## Architecture
- Single entry point: `backend/index.php` dispatches via `?action=` parameter
- Endpoints in `backend/endpoints/`, each loaded via `require_once`
- PDO singleton via `getDB()` in `db.php`
- Utility functions in `helpers.php`

## Coding Standards
- PSR-12 enforced by PHP-CS-Fixer. Run `composer cs-fix` before committing
- `declare(strict_types=1)` in all new endpoint files
- Use typed properties and return types
- Short array syntax, no unused imports

## Database
- All queries use PDO prepared statements — never interpolate values into SQL
- Connection: `PDO::ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES => false` for real prepared statements
- Error mode: `PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION`
- Fetch mode: `PDO::FETCH_ASSOC`

## Security
- All user input sanitized via `sanitizeString()` (decode → strip → trim)
- URLs validated for http/https scheme via `filter_var`
- Employer submissions use `strip_tags` + `htmlspecialchars` with ENT_QUOTES
- CORS allowlist in `index.php` — add new origins to `$allowedOrigins`

## Responses
- All responses use `respondJson()` which sets status, Content-Type, encodes JSON, and exits
- Error responses: `{'error': 'message'}` with appropriate HTTP status
- Never expose stack traces or SQL in production error messages
